<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31176" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρεσία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίη</span>, ἡ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρέσσω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rowing, oarage</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρῶτα μὲν εἰρεσίη, μετέπειτα δὲ
					κάλλιμος οὖρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.640
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρεσίῃ χρᾶσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.203
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				4.110
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρεσίας ζυγόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					249
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ. τῶν τριήρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mete.</u>
					369b10
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ. πτερῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Tim.</u>
					40
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρὰ δ᾽ εἰρεσίᾳ μαστῶν ἕπεται
				Ἀστυάναξ</span> close to her <i>throbbing</i> breast,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				570
			</span></i> (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρεσίῃ γλώσσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dionys.Eleg.
					4.3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>oar</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.352
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				385
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in
			collective sense, <i>rowers, oarsmen</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1453
			</span></i>(lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.287
			</span></i> (Antip.(?)); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξυνέχειν τὴν
			εἰ</span>. keep <i>the oars</i> together or make <i>the
				rowers</i> keep time, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>boat-song, to which the rowers kept time</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλεῖν εἰρεσίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					32
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>VH</u>
				1.40
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> pl.,
				<i>rowers' benches</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.21.2
			</span></i>. (The 
				Ep.
			 form, due to metrical lengthening, is retained in
		Prose.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
